{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558916-awakening-s-orders-in-ascension","id":1558916,"title":"Awakening's Orders in Ascension?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-18T01:16:19-07:00","id":1558916,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Awakening's Orders in Ascension?","content":"I've had some thoughts about how one would go about backporting the orders from Mage: the Awakening into Mage: the Ascension, so I thought I'd share them and get some feedback. See what others think. <hr /><br /> If you decide what to do with the Pentacle based on their praxis, then they should go to the Order of Hermes. While people's old complaints/jokes about only being able to be Hermetics in Awakening were overdone, it is pretty undeniable that the game draws heavily from Hermeticism and Hermeticism-adjacent or Hermeticism-descended magical thought for it's framework. You still have a few different options about how to integrate the Pentacle into the Order of Hermes though.<ul><li>You could give them their own major house, or minor house in Ex Miscellanea if you want the Pentacle to be small. Probably call it House Draconis? Defining feature is a variant of the Hermetic paradigm which believes in a magocratic civilization Before Time, commonly called Atlantis, and conceives of the Platonic realm as the Supernal. I'd associate them with the Time sphere, given Awakening's focus on the Exarchs and Archmages retconning history/reality in their war for ascension.</li> <li>Alternatively, you could give each order it's own house. A militant House Adamant for the Arrows, a secretive House Labrys for the Guardians, a stereotypical bookworm House Pancryptios for the Mysterium, a religious House Thearch for the Silver Ladder, and... honestly I think you'd just have to roll the Free Council into House Thig. Speaking of...</li> <li>You could merge the orders with Hermetic Houses. Free Council with House Thig/House Verditius or maybe House Solificati, Guardians of the Veil with either House Janissary or House Quaesitor, Mysterium with House Bonisagus or House Shaea, Adamantine Arrow with House Flambeau or House Tytalus, and Silver Ladder with House Quaesitor or House Fortunae.</li> <li>You could also make the Pentacle, or the Pentacle's orders, into inter-house organization(s).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> If you're deciding what to do with the Pentacle based on their in-universe history, then you'll find they have quite a bit in common with the Euthanatoi/Chakravanti and the Cult of Ecstasy/Sahajiya. The Diamond originates through the synthesis of Greek, Persian, Egyptian and Indian magical traditions in the Hellenistic world following Alexander the Great's conquests and death. These four 'great cults' - the Arcadian Mysteries, the Karpani, the Mantra Sadhaki, and the Weret-Hekau - all had compatible understandings of magical cosmology that reflected the setting's objective truth; ancient fallen utopia (Atlantis), evil gods vs good gods (Exarchs vs Oracles), a higher celestial realm of pure forms (Supernal Realm), and five paths/ten arcana a mage can follow.<br /> <br /> From the Mantra Sadhaki emerged four 'darshana' which were the forerunners of the Adamantine Arrows, the Guardians of the Veil, the Mysterium (who would split into two different orders before recombining again later), and the Silver Ladder. There was also a fifth outsider sect, the Ajivaki, who were the proto-Free Council. And the model of the darshanas either spread very prolifically or is based on a Supernal truth that all mage societies spontaneously organize themselves into.<br /> So, what does the above mean? It means that, if you're bringing the Pentacle into Ascension based on their histories, then they should be just as involved with the Chakravanti, Sahajiya, Taftani and the Batini as they are with the Hermetics. Some options:<ul><li>Make the Diamond Order an independent Craft, or Tradition if you can figure out how to give them a Sphere seat without replacing somebody else (or if you're okay with the Diamond replacing someone), whose history interweaves with the aforementioned mage organizations. For additional historicity, I'd say to associate them with the Indo-Greek kingdoms, Graeco-Buddhism, and Manichaeism.<ul><li>As for the Free Council, you could make them a sub-faction who either joined recently or always remained on the fringe of the Craft... or you could make them another independent Craft in their own right. Say they're technomancers who rejected an offer to join/resisted absorption by the Technocracy. Maybe put them in the Disparate Alliance. Maybe make them like a non-Goth version of the Hollow Ones, since the Free Council are <i>culture mages</i> as well as <i>techno-mages</i>.</li> </ul></li> <li>Alternatively, fuse the Pentacle orders into the aforementioned Traditions. If you wanted to put them all in one Tradition, I'd go with the Cult of Ecstasy. They might not seem like they fit, but I actually think that the Supernal, the Paths, Mage Sight, etc are pretty compatible with Lakashim, Ananda, etc. And I already mentioned that I think Time is the sphere that fits Awakening mages the best. The Pentacle orders would definitely lean more towards the less transgressive, right-handed path of tantra, but there is canon precendent for members doing drugs, engaging in BDSM practices, etc in pursuit of greater insight into magic. If you wanted to split the orders between the Traditions, then my advice would be as such:<ul><li>The Adamantine Arrow might seem like they belong with the Akashics, what with them being martial art wizards, but this is a bit of a trap. The Arrows are all about ascension through struggle, and would find themselves an uneasy fit in the balance and harmony-focused Akashayana. I'd make them one of the more open combat-focused Euthanatoi subfactions, akin to the Knights of Radamanthys.</li> <li>The Guardians of the Veil fit extremely well into the Euthanatoi, Awakening's Legacy based on the Chakravanti - the Thread Cutters - is exclusive to Guardians. The Legacy based on the Ahl-i-Batin - the Subtle Ones - is also Guardian exclusive though, they might be able to fit there too. I'd definitely tie their history into the Ixoi, the Golden Chalice, and the Batini regardless of where you put them.</li> <li>The Silver Chalice would... honestly I'm not entirely sure if I <i>get</i> the Silver Chalice. They're the social splat. They don't necessarily have any inherent beliefs about what magic is or how to achieve ascension, they just think that 'magic is the birthright of humanity' and that eventually everyone should awaken in the utopian magocracy they want to build. They could probably fit into any Tradition really, since they're defined by a political goal more than a paradigmatic belief.</li> <li>The Mysterium believes that magic is alive, that it hides itself, and that it needs to be found in the mundane world and protected. They have subfactions which interpret this in different ways, e.g. some think that magic is God, some subscribe to a kind of chaos magic meme theory, etc. Their beliefs don't translate perfectly into Ascension cosmology, but they still work fairly well. In terms of where they'd go, they fit well with the Hermetics due to being the kind of classical wizard scholarly stereotype. But magic being alive also fits pretty well with the Ectstatics or the Batini. Or the Verbena, though they'd definitely be an odd cultural fit there.</li> <li>The Free Council are an odd fit with the rest of the Pentacle even in their own canon. My previously mentioned thoughts still apply; you could make them a formerly independent Craft that recently joined up with the Diamond Orders. Or say they are explicitly descended from the Ajivaki and were always part of the Pentacle, but were defined by being outsiders and loyal opposition. But I think they'd be better off made into their own Craft. One that has relations and history with the Diamond, but ultimately unrelated.</li> <li>With the Awakened mage's worldview of Supernal Truth vs Abyssal Lie, their canonical partial descent from Persian mages, their view of ascension being one-and-the-same with growth in magical power... they all have some compatibility with the Taftani. I feel they're a little too different for fusing them with the Taftani to work, but they should definitely have strong ties.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Another way to look at things, which I think might be interesting and potentially fruitful but don't have the wherewithal to do myself, would be to identify what features of magic are unique to Awakening and make them the focuses that you build the Pentacle around.<br /> <br /> <br /> A few other scattershot thoughts:<ul><li>The Tremere liches. If you wanted to incorporate them into Ascension, I see two options. Number one, make them members of House Tremere who found a way to stall their transformation into Kindred by eating people's souls. Number two, keep the backstory from Awakening but replace the Tremere name with something else. Maybe fuse them with the Consanguinity of Joy?</li> <li>The Banishers. &quot;Mages whose awakening went wrong and left them traumatized instead of enlightened, now they view magic - including their own - as fundamentally wrong and hunt other mages&quot; is a concept that still works without the rest of the cosmological baggage of Awakening. You can have them in Ascension if you want, they'd just be considered a subtype of Marauder instead of their own thing.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":".  Fixing typos 03-18-2026, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T02:23:30-07:00","id":1558918,"title":"","content":"I think the Orders are just fundamentally different types of organisation to the Traditions. They all have beliefs about the cosmology of the setting, but they don't really represent different ways to do magic as much as how magic is supposed to be used. Like, the Guardians have a belief system around reincarnation similar to the Euthanatos, but their magic doesn't itself rely on that belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T07:12:38-07:00","id":1558920,"title":"","content":"Another possibility is that they could be cross-Tradition camps or organizations that represent philosophies and relationships to magic/power. Most of the core principles and approaches of the Orders, such as &quot;Magic must be Protected&quot; and &quot;Magic Through Service and Struggle&quot; would fit well as ideologies in the Traditions in general. The Guardian's of the Veil might need some tweaking as hiding magic isn't a great way to keep it in the Consensus. That said, there are indications that catastrophic paradox backlashes can drive ideas completely out of the Consensus, so preventing major breaches while pushing magic in small and subtle ways would still fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T07:30:58-07:00","id":1558921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558916-awakening-s-orders-in-ascension?p=1558920#post1558920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility is that they could be cross-Tradition camps or organizations that represent philosophies and relationships to magic/power. Most of the core principles and approaches of the Orders, such as &quot;Magic must be Protected&quot; and &quot;Magic Through Service and Struggle&quot; would fit well as ideologies in the Traditions in general. The Guardian's of the Veil might need some tweaking as hiding magic isn't a great way to keep it in the Consensus. That said, there are indications that catastrophic paradox backlashes can drive ideas completely out of the Consensus, so preventing major breaches while pushing magic in small and subtle ways would still fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing about the Guardians' Labyrinths is that they teach fake magic/truths in order to lead sleepers and the unworthy away from discovering true magic. In Ascension I think emphasis would be placed on &quot;teaching non-True magic&quot; aspect. Labyrinths would be carefully managed movements that genuinely do try to work supernatural beliefs into the consensus, they just focus on beliefs that are unlikely to cause someone to Awaken unless they meet the Guardian's standards. Lots of 'mundane' magical thinking, maybe a little bit of Linear Magic for those they trust. Stuff that won't provoke Paradox.<br /> <br /> ...which means that the Guardians of the Veil might be responsible for a bunch of conspiracy theories. Which is unfortunate. But also something that might be true in Awakening too, not just when translating them into Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-20T04:32:12-07:00","id":1558947,"title":"","content":"Sorry to double post, but I had another thought.<br /> <br /> Mage: the Awakening takes quite a bit from Theosophy. This is probably more a result of Theosophy being extraordinarily influential on western culture's views of the occult, 'eastern' religions, etc, and in Theosophy drawing from quite a few of the same places as Awakening, than the result of Awakening's authors specifically wanting it to be a Theosophical game. However, the similarities remain nonetheless. So, another way to work the Pentacle into Ascension, is for them to be a Craft with an explicitly Theosophical paradigm. Any claims they make to ancient origins are just that - claims. They're actually a very young organisation, which only the Free Council subfaction is honest about.<br /> <br /> Of course, if we apply this same logic to Ascension's own Traditions, then the Akashayana should also be Theosophists, the Verbena should be Wiccans, and the Order of Hermes should be Neo-Hermetics instead of classical Hermetics.<br /> <br /> Still, it's <i>a way</i> you could use the Orders in Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-20T06:48:35-07:00","id":1558948,"title":"","content":"The Akashayana <i>are</i> theosophists, at least in large part, which is why they are named after the Akashic Record and have a history that originates with Mt Meru. Actually, they aren't the only ones as the Celestial Chorus has some strong theosophical basis as well.<br /> <br /> Even though the Traditions are supposed to be one part magical stereotype (wizard, witch, martial artist, cleric, etc.) and one part based on historical groups, a lot of them also take heavy inspiration from 19th and 20th century occult, spiritual, or anthropological ideas. Having the Pentacle based on modern ideas but also being really old is just par for the course for Ascension, but... the well you are having them draw from has already been drawn from quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T14:56:53-07:00","id":1561785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558916-awakening-s-orders-in-ascension?p=1558921#post1558921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the thing about the Guardians' Labyrinths is that they teach fake magic/truths in order to lead sleepers and the unworthy away from discovering true magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the mandate of the Guardians is at all compatible with the Traditions. To fit, they'd have to change more radically what they do and why, even if keeping the methods. Or have a decidedly antagonistic role in the game.<br /> <br /> They could be Technocratic saboteurs, working from within the Council to further the goals of the Union. Maybe agents of Threat Null, targets of the mental shenanigans of Control. Or could be a faction that abandoned the goals of mass Ascension after finding some evidence that it's going to backfire royally.<br /> <br /> As Agents of the Union they could be either the result of Conditioning, could be full infiltrators using hidden tech to perform &quot;magic&quot;, or just common Mages that sold out for profit, power, blackmail, etc. Could also be agents of other groups, Ghouls protecting the Masquerade or Kinfolk preserving the Veil, their actual loyalty isn't with the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Control has the twist of an alien mind that will behave like the 1st Ed Technocracy, but won't really have to make a lot of sense. They're an infection, a spiritual threat that commands the Mages and change their worldview. What those affected will become in the end is unknown. A different supernatural threat can give the same results, like an ancient vampire, other kind of spirit or some new manifestation of Paradox.<br /> <br /> Hidden defectors, they discovered a secret of reality that fundamentally contradicts current Magic/Enlightened theories. The game is full of those, things the Traditions take for granted, but actually aren't a certainty. What Avatars are after all? What is Paradox and where it comes from? What are Reality Zones? What is really moving the &quot;Consensus&quot;? Are all Mages really the same phenomenon?<br /> <br /> You can pick any of those. They all have fairly consistent and coherent explanations, but also edge cases that don't really fit with the model. Take one and turn on its head, make an answer that completely reframes the whole Ascension War. It being right is irrelevant, the Guardians think it is and will fight to keep the world even more ignorant than the Union already tries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T18:03:31-07:00","id":1561797,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> I had just adapted the Orders as factions within the Nine Mystic Traditions. The Adamantine Arrow as those focused on pursuing the Ascension War against the Technocracy and Nephandi via direct action; the Silver Chalice as those who focus on cultivating power and influence within the mundane world (both as a way of pursing the Ascension War and for personal gain); the Mysterium as those focused on research and intellectual pursuits as well as preserving the world's mystical heritage; and the Guardians of the Veil as those focused on policing the Traditions for internal corruption and safeguarding the mundane world from the dangers of the Awakened one; with the Free Council as an outside group of assorted Orphans, Rogues, and other outcasts and pariahs organizing for self-protection and getting to have a say in events. Mostly this was just a way to give my PCs factions to potentially join or otherwise play off of as they grew in power/influence from a local scale to a more regional or global one, depending on whether the group wanted a game more focused on combat, politics, esoterica, or espionage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T03:02:26-07:00","id":1561812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558916-awakening-s-orders-in-ascension?p=1561797#post1561797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Chalice</div> </div> </div> </div>Just FYI, it's the Silver Ladder. I assume Crying was just misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T03:26:36-07:00","id":1561813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558916-awakening-s-orders-in-ascension?p=1561812#post1561812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just FYI, it's the Silver Ladder. I assume Crying was just misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was assuming it was a deliberate name change since Silver Ladder doesn't make a lot of sense without a mythic ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T06:08:30-07:00","id":1561820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558916-awakening-s-orders-in-ascension?p=1561813#post1561813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was assuming it was a deliberate name change since Silver Ladder doesn't make a lot of sense without a mythic ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you could be right.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure that's true. The Thearchs use ladders as a metaphor for their slightly more benevolent version of the great chain of being. I don't think you'd need that double-meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}